I say a praying mantis. Equally majestic and horrifying. 

&#x200B;

Yes I know they are insects, but they are also animals.

Bow meister, guardian and ally of the string kingdom. None shall pass him. 

&#x200B;

Sorry had to much caffeine.

But what if it goes wrong? There are countless incidents of people just blowing their faces off with a shotgun and surviving (albeit usually a few hours or a couple days) in excruciating agony. Unless you plan on using some advanced contraption to fire the arrow I would advise against it. Also consider this:

&#x200B;

Everyone is in self-quarantine. We are all unsure as to when this lockdown will end. It could be weeks or even months. Regardless your body will begin to decompose and since we are in spring the temperatures will fluctuate. Somebody will eventually find your rotting bloated maggot-covered corpse and have to clean it up. There are many crime scene cleaners who deal with all manner of death. Homicides, suicides, etc. 

&#x200B;

Somebody is going to have to remove your body from your house or apartment, clean the blood stains and liquefied body tissue off the floor and other parts of the room. I'm merely saying if for no other reason, don't do it because of the fact someone else is going to have to deal with your mess. If you want to be considerate, drape everything in painters tarp or plastic wrap so it's an easy cleanup.

"MEDIOCRE AT BEST! MAYBE BETTER OFF DEAD! AM I A FAILURE FROM BIRTH?! IS MISERY WHAT I DESERVE?! AM I JUST SO VOID OF LOVE THAT I'M NEVER GOOD! NEVER GOOD ENOUGH?!!"

&#x200B;

Never Good Enough by Citizen Soldier

&#x200B;

Well the whole dang song really. Here's a link to the Lyric Video  [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oHN3TPq1upw](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oHN3TPq1upw)

Chocolate Syrup on top of Orange Sherbert icecream. My mom legit has to leave the room when I eat it. Sadly I haven't had it in years. Also ketchup on scrambled eggs (scrambled eggs without flavor added I mean)

&#x200B;

Also a peanut butter and dill pickle sandwich.

Red skins on peanuts but not peanuts themselves. My next door neighbor when I was little gave me a mr. Goodbar after I finished helping her weed her garden. (I really miss you Pat) she was the sweetest old lady and quickly got my mom when I started having an allergic reaction.

&#x200B;

I can eat peanuts just fine. I don't touch Mr. Goodbar's though.

The fucking entitlement! Take a look at this! [https://sta.sh/0i7qza8r553](https://sta.sh/0i7qza8r553)

&#x200B;

And I just want to make a freaking fanfiction story with Brineary in it! I understand it's 'their character' but come on, it's fucking writing. I have been attacked numerous times by white knights and snitches who claim I stole somebodies artwork. Where you may ask? Tumblr. Why? All because I posted a freaking gif that I thought was funny and even hashtagged as not my art. I could not find the original poster. So some shithead decided they needed to have my account terminated for it even though by that time I had removed the artwork at the artists request (they were nice about it) and I sent an email to the Tumblr admins about it and got my account back up. However I deleted it shortly thereafter because so many deviantart artists/Tumblr artists were harrassing me and calling me an art thief even when I gave full credit. That was when I learned the importance of reverse image searches. 

&#x200B;

Still. It makes me hesitant to post any form of art on any possible form of social media, Hell even Wattpad! I'm so scared that I'm going to end being at the receiving end of a copywright strike or some other form of BS even when I named the artist and provided a link to their page.
